From 2cfaa19191e54ba4d7509a687b00a406224fcf03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vaishnavi220506 <183067453+Vaishnavi220506@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 00:31:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Adopt upstream PR #56444: carry PLE input ids through PP
 intermediates

Makes PLE pipeline-rank-free by transporting int32 input_ids inside the
existing intermediate tensors (+4 B/token per hop). Removes the PP>1
rejections on both backends. Strictly supersedes our local patch 2
(rank-0 confinement).

Fixed from the PR as merged here: the three new PP tests import both
backends in one process and collide registering
vllm::qwen4_exp_grouped_gemma_rmsnorm (amd and nvidia model.py each do
it). Added @spawn_new_process_for_each_test, the same guard the file
already uses for the analogous mtp tests.

Upstream-PR: vllm-project/vllm#56444 (Vaishnavi220506, pending)
